# An allowlist. The Dockerfiles that copy the repository (`COPY . ...`)
# build and test from source inside the container, and must get only what
# is named below -- never .git, an editor's folder, or whatever untracked
# file (a key, a .env) happens to sit in a working tree.
#
# A new top-level file or folder the containers need is added here; until
# it is, they don't see it.
#
# Left out on purpose: target/ (host build output, gigabytes; the
# containers build into their own), dist/ (reaches the containers that need
# it as a bind mount or a named build context), build-hardware-tests/,
# .git/, .github/, and the files only a contributor reads.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!build.rs
!rust-toolchain.toml
!LICENSE
!README.md

!src
!tests
!include
!examples
!docs
!fuzz
!scripts
!docker
!packaging
!debian
